{"duration_api_ms":1183251,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"071f53fd-ac78-41fc-9e28-324d52d871af","total_cost_usd":7.5897846,"usage":{"input_tokens":376,"cache_creation_input_tokens":211984,"cache_read_input_tokens":29161873,"output_tokens":81271,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":40789},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":211984,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3611,"cache_read_input_tokens":227211,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1797,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1797},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":63697,"outputTokens":2463,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":2,"costUSD":0.096012,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":376,"outputTokens":81271,"cacheReadInputTokens":29161873,"cacheCreationInputTokens":211984,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":7.493772599999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":40789,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":224,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"blocked\",\"summary\":\"Established and verified a working site-to-site IPsec tunnel between node1 (VyOS) and node2 (OPNsense) carrying both private LANs (node3's 10.50.1.0/24 behind node1, node4's 10.50.2.0/24 behind node2) over the transit network (172.16.0.0/30), so node3 and node4 reach each other by private address with traffic encrypted in transit (confirmed via growing ESP SA packet/byte counters). Mandatory restart-and-recovery evidence was fully captured for node1 and node2 (the actual IPsec endpoints): both were rebooted one at a time, showed a changed boot identity, and came back with the tunnel, firewall, and interfaces auto-restored, with node3-node4 connectivity re-verified afterward. However, node3 and node4 (Alpine leaf nodes) did not come back within the session after their reboot commands were acknowledged and executed (roughly 2+ hours and 1+ hour of polling respectively, both showing a persistent \\\"connection reset by peer\\\" rather than the normal boot-then-recover pattern seen on node1/node2) - restart persistence for node3 and node4 could not be confirmed and is reported here as an explicit limitation rather than claimed.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Mapped physical topology via link probing: node1 eth0/node2 vtnet0 = shared control network; node1 eth2 <-> node3 eth1 = lan-a; node1 eth1 <-> node2 vtnet1 = transit; node2 vtnet2 <-> node4 eth1 = lan-b\",\"Configured node1 (VyOS): eth1=172.16.0.1/30 (transit), eth2=10.50.1.1/24 (lan-a); committed and saved\",\"Configured node1 IPsec site-to-site (IKEv2, AES256/SHA256/DH14, PSK) peer NODE2, tunnel local 10.50.1.0/24 / remote 10.50.2.0/24; committed and saved\",\"Assigned node2 (OPNsense) interfaces opt1 (vtnet1 TRANSIT 172.16.0.2/30) and opt2 (vtnet2 LAN_B 10.50.2.1/24) by editing config.xml and running configctl interface reconfigure\",\"Generated a temporary root API key on node2 (later deleted) to drive the OPNsense IPsec REST API: created connection, local/remote PSK auth (id=transit IPs), child SA (local 10.50.2.0/24 / remote 10.50.1.0/24), pre-shared key entry, enabled IPsec, reconfigured the service\",\"Added OPNsense firewall pass rules for IKE/NAT-T/ESP on opt1 from node1, LAN_B traffic on opt2, and decrypted tunnel traffic on enc0 to LAN_B; reloaded the filter\",\"Configured node3 and node4 (Alpine) eth1 static addresses (10.50.1.2/24, 10.50.2.2/24) and routes to the other private subnet via their router, persisted in /etc/network/interfaces\",\"Verified end-to-end encrypted connectivity: node3 pinged node4's private address and vice versa, with ESP SA packet/byte counters on node1 incrementing to confirm traffic traversed the tunnel\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id/boottime, SA state, connectivity) on all 4 nodes\",\"Restarted node1 one at a time; confirmed new boot_id, interfaces/IPsec config persisted, tunnel re-established automatically, and node3<->node4 connectivity restored\",\"Restarted node2 one at a time; confirmed new kern.boottime, interfaces/pf/IPsec config persisted, tunnel re-established automatically, and node3<->node4 connectivity restored\",\"Attempted to restart node3 then node4 one at a time; both acknowledged the reboot command but did not become reachable again during the session despite extensive polling, so their post-restart boot identity and recovery could not be verified\",\"Removed the temporary OPNsense API key from node2 after configuration was complete\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"IPsec tunnel established between node1 and node2 over the transit network\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c0b6e1b294aa4ddb\",\"cmd-de999d347cd5444a\",\"cmd-868213a12ca44daf\",\"cmd-c5a9edb2a7e04af4\",\"cmd-2e2fee0d8dce4bcc\",\"cmd-43e1a289a2a247fb\",\"cmd-ab8a92c0d1c5470a\"],\"summary\":\"VyOS site-to-site peer NODE2 and OPNsense Swanctl connection/local/remote/child/PSK configured and committed; swanctl --list-sas on both node1 and node2 shows an ESTABLISHED IKEv2 SA and INSTALLED tunnel child SA between 172.16.0.1 and 172.16.0.2.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 and node4 reach each other by private address with traffic encrypted in transit\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5758478622614da4\",\"cmd-9a8e8a6dbe85404c\",\"cmd-dfebf8857b724a3b\"],\"summary\":\"node3 (10.50.1.2) pings node4 (10.50.2.2) and vice versa with 0% loss; node1's ESP SA counters increment from 0 to growing packet/byte counts concurrently with the pings, confirming the traffic traverses the encrypted tunnel rather than a direct path.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Firewall/NAT allows the tunnel traffic (OPNsense default-deny)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-feb97fcc90ff4ee9\",\"cmd-6df266ddddaa4c48\",\"cmd-7a75daa7f96f4537\"],\"summary\":\"Added OPNsense pass rules for IKE/NAT-T/ESP on opt1 and decrypted tunnel traffic to LAN_B on enc0; reloaded filter; confirmed node1 could then reach node2's LAN_B gateway address 10.50.2.1.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Configuration persists (survives reboot) on VyOS and OPNsense\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c0b6e1b294aa4ddb\",\"cmd-fe5c27ab8768429a\",\"cmd-3ed25f191c774aef\"],\"summary\":\"VyOS config committed+saved to config.boot; OPNsense interfaces/IPsec/firewall written directly to the live config.xml store (no separate save step required).\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: healthy baseline captured\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c461eefeae1e4c3d\"],\"summary\":\"Captured node1 boot_id 32669db3-... and ESTABLISHED/INSTALLED IPsec SA state before restart.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: acknowledgement returns before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-32cece08ad8e4c05\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded reboot command on node1 returned 'reboot scheduled' immediately.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: changed boot identity proven\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-158974b49d6640f3\",\"cmd-ef0306e4a6a24ce8\"],\"summary\":\"node1 became unreachable (connection timed out) then returned with boot_id 4d7f696d-... , different from the pre-restart 32669db3-... baseline.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: recovered state and cluster function verified\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-70f2e174057d40d1\",\"cmd-608f0e90a7ad4a1a\"],\"summary\":\"Post-restart, eth1/eth2 addresses and the IPsec connection were present without reconfiguration, an ESTABLISHED SA and INSTALLED tunnel reappeared automatically, and node
